---
import data from '../data/events.json';
const bySources = data.sources;
const mainstream = bySources.filter((s) => s.circuit === 'mainstream');
const diaspora = bySources.filter((s) => s.circuit === 'diaspora');
const platform = bySources.filter((s) => s.circuit === 'platform');
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>About — NYC Indian Dance</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>💃</text></svg>" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p><a href="/">← Back to the calendar</a></p>
      <h1>About this calendar</h1>
      <p>
        Indian dance in New York is listed in two worlds that don't talk to each
        other. Community listings carry the festivals and recitals but miss what
        the big presenters put on; the mainstream venues present world-class
        Indian artists but never file them anywhere you'd think to look. Ten
        events can happen at ten different venues in a year with no single place
        that knew about all ten.
      </p>
      <p>
        This calendar merges both worlds. Automated sweeps read the calendars of
        the venues and presenters below several times a week, a broader search
        looks for events beyond them, and every listing is checked before it
        appears here — working links, a real date, a price. Each event links to
        its <em>info page</em> and its <em>ticket page</em> separately, and shows
        every source it was found in. The source is always authoritative.
      </p>
      <h2>What's included</h2>
      <p>
        Indian dance in all its forms — Kathak, Bharatanatyam, Odissi, Kuchipudi,
        Mohiniyattam, Manipuri, Sattriya, Kathakali, folk, Bollywood, and
        Indian-rooted fusion and contemporary work — plus dance talks and
        workshops, across the five boroughs, New Jersey, Long Island and
        Westchester. Pure music concerts are out of scope.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources watched</h2>
      <p><strong>Presenters &amp; venues:</strong> {mainstream.map((s) => s.name).join(' · ')}</p>
      <p><strong>Community circuit:</strong> {diaspora.map((s) => s.name).join(' · ')}</p>
      <p><strong>Platforms:</strong> {platform.map((s) => s.name).join(' · ')}</p>
      <h2>Subscribe</h2>
      <p>
        Add the whole calendar to Google or Apple Calendar with the
        <a href="/calendar.ics">calendar feed</a>. A short weekly email digest is
        coming; subscription details will appear here.
      </p>
      <p class="fine">
        Spotted a mistake, or want your event listed? Every listing improves the
        calendar for everyone — contact details coming with the newsletter.
      </p>
    </main>
    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --bg: #faf7f2; --ink: #2b2118; --muted: #7a6a5c; --accent: #b3512f; --line: #e8dfd3;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --bg: #191411; --ink: #f0e7dc; --muted: #a89a8a; --accent: #e07a4f; --line: #3a3129; }
      }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; }
      main { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
      h1 { font-family: Georgia, serif; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
      h2 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      .fine { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 1rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
